og --diff` traced backwards), a click opens the preview, double-click shows the commit; at most searched revisions (`issues.blameLinks.maxRevisions`, 1–5000); update the tracker on start and finish (`issues.syncState`, #1266, quick toggle; off = “Start” and “Finish” change nothing in the tracker): after the branch “Start” sets the state (`issues.startState`, empty = do not change; GitHub: label), assigns to me (`issues.assignOnStart`) and comments (`issues.startComment`, empty = no comment), result as a row in the messages view, an error leaves the branch in place; “Finish” (status panel, context menu, button of the preview) shows the dialog “Finish ATL-123” with the target state from `issues.endStates` and “Keep state”, comment from `issues.endComment` (the unchanged default follows the language of the IDE) with `{branch}`, `{commits}`, `{pr}`, `{time}`, `{kennung}` (`\n` = new line) and “Hand over to …”; without “Send” nothing is written, the dialog shows errors (403, 400) with the tracker''s text; in the preview “Write a comment …” (Markdown, Ctrl+Enter sends); YouTrack via `POST /api/commands` with the state field (`issues.stateField`) and user field (`issues.assigneeField`), GitHub via comment and PATCH (labels, assignees, “Done” closes); state field, user field, state on start and target states per connection in `issues.connections` (`stateField`, `assigneeField`, `startState`, `endStates`), otherwise the global values; drop-down lists “Load values from tracker”; track time per issue (`issues.timeTracking`, #1267, quick toggle, off = neither display nor file nor dialog): the clock runs while an issue is current and the IDE is active (input, debugger run), idle time beyond `issues.idleMinutes` stops it and is not counted; status panel “ATL-123 · 1:25” with pause/resume, reset, correct; storage per issue and day in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Atlas\time.json` (file lock, several IDEs do not count twice); on finishing or switching “… book?” with duration (rounded to `issues.timeRounding` minutes), work type and description, buttons Book, Later, Discard; YouTrack as a work item, GitHub optionally as a comment “Effort: …”; command *Pending time entries …*; checklists in the preview (`issues.preview.checklists`, #1273): task lists of the description (`- [ ]`, `* [x]`, `1. [ ]`, also indented, not in code blocks) as ticks with “3/5” in the header; ticking loads the current description, checks the line (text and position), changes only `[ ]`/`[x]` and writes back (YouTrack `POST /api/issues/<key>`, GitHub `PATCH …/issues/<n>`); if it has changed in the meantime, Atlas writes nothing and reloads; “Add item …” appends `- [ ] text`; without write permission read-only, checklists in comments read-only; off = list as text; progress of the current issue in the status panel (`issues.checklistStatus`, row `atlas.issue.checklist` “ATL-131 · 3/5”, a click opens the preview at the list, without a checklist no row); links as a tree (`issues.preview.links`, #1279): depends on, blocks, subtasks with progress (2/3), parent, duplicates, “relates to” and mentions collapsed, per row icon (open, done, blocked), key, title and state, plus “Create subtask …” and “Link …” (YouTrack and GitHub; off: flat list); warning on “Start” as long as a “depends on” issue is open (`issues.warnBlocked`); board (`issues.board`, #1272, *Atlas.Board*, View › Atlas › Board): dock window “Atlas board” with the columns of the agile board (YouTrack, board and sprint selectable, “current sprint” preselected) or of the GitHub project (status field, iterations as sprints; without a project or without the permission `read:project` Open/Closed with a note), cards with key, title, initials of the assignee, priority stripe, checklist progress and lock; “Mine only”/“All” (`issues.board.onlyMine` = filter on opening), search, refresh; dragging into another column asks (`issues.board.confirmMove`, “Don''t ask again” switches it off) with an optional comment and writes via the same ways as “Finish” (YouTrack `POST /api/commands`, GitHub `updateProjectV2ItemFieldValue` or closing/reopening), on error the card jumps back; double-click opens the preview, context menu Start, Open in browser, Assign to me; the current issue is highlighted; narrow (below 360 pixels) as a list grouped by columns; last state in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Atlas\issues\<tracker>-board.json`, offline with a note; sprint tile (#1277): burndown with actual line, dashed ideal line, mark “today” and tooltip per day (`issues.sprint.burndown`), comparison with the previous sprint (pale line normalized to sprint days, “done 5 · previous sprint 4 on the same day ▲1”) and velocity of the last three sprints as bars (`issues.sprint.compare`; off = no earlier sprint is queried; finished sprints queried once and cached as `<tracker>-sprint-<board>-<sprint>.json`); search issues in the command palette (`issues.paletteSearch`, #1270): `#text` or `ATL-text` searches in the tracker, `#42` or `ATL-12` reads the issue directly, an empty `#` shows the recently opened ones without a network query; Enter preview, Ctrl+Enter Start, Shift+Enter browser, Ctrl+C copy key; comment editor (`issues.commentEditor`, #1278) in the preview and in the finish dialog: “@” suggests users of the tracker (YouTrack login and name, GitHub assignable users), “#” or `ATL-` issues; arrows, Enter or Tab, Esc; Ctrl+B bold, Ctrl+I italic, Ctrl+Shift+K code block, “Preview” with the renderer of the issue preview; drafts per tracker, issue and field in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Atlas\issues\drafts.json` (2 s after the last change and on closing, deleted after sending); off = plain text field; table “Snippets” (`issues.commentSnippets`, name and text with `{issue}`, `{branch}`, `{commit}`, `{version}`), inserted with Ctrl+Space or “Snippet ▾”; unchanged defaults follow the language of the IDE (#1458); tab “Development” with branches and commits for the key, pull requests with CI traffic light or linked changes and changed units, searched only when the tab is opened (`issues.preview.development`); messages about my issues (`issues.notify`, #1271, quick toggle): every connection (tracker of the `.atlas` and `issues.connections`) is asked for changes in the background (YouTrack: changed issues and their activities, GitHub: `/notifications` conditionally with If-Modified-Since), new comments by others, assignments and state changes appear combined per issue in the notification center (source “Issues”, pop up, only collect or off like other sources), “Open” shows the issue in “Atlas issue” at the first new comment, affected issues carry a dot in “My issues” until they were opened; Atlas does not report own changes, on first switching on “now” applies; only with an active IDE (minimized or 30 min without input pauses, caught up once afterwards), additionally when “My issues” is opened; an error (token refused, unreachable) comes once and not again until the next success; interval (`issues.notify.intervalMinutes`, 2–1440; doubled after errors up to 60 minutes, GitHub at least X-Poll-Interval), scope (`issues.notify.scope`: assigned, assignedOrCreated, watched); “Attach to issue …” (`issues.attach`, #1276, quick toggle; Atlas menu, *Atlas.IssueAttach* in the palette, “Attach …” in the window “Atlas issue”, row `atlas.issue.attach` in the status panel below the current issue): screenshot of the running program (main window of the debugged process or chosen by click) and form in the designer with frame, arrow and blacking out, log file (on request only the last lines), debug note (location, excerpt, call stack, last exception; values of secret names as ***) and exception history in one step; the dialog shows names and sizes, sending happens only with “Send”; YouTrack uploads the files (`POST /api/issues/<key>/attachments`) and on request writes a comment with references, GitHub gets texts as a code block in the comment, pictures are on the clipboard (note “Paste in GitHub with Ctrl+V”) and the browser opens the issue; files stay in `%TEMP%\Atlas\attach` only until sending or cancelling; log files to suggest (`issues.attach.logFiles`, separated by “;”, with `$(ProjectDir)`, `$(ProjectName)`, environment variables and `*`), pictures at most this wide (`issues.attach.maxImageWidth`, 320–7680) | empty, branch, empty, empty, `{kennung} `, on, none, none, none, on, on, on, on, on, on, on, 200, on, on, State, Assignee, empty, off, empty, empty, `Done in {branch}.\n{commits}` (German IDE: `Erledigt in {branch}.\n{commits}`), off, 10, 5, on, on, on, on, on, on, on, on, on, on, on, two snippets (English IDE: “Please check with the current build”, “Fixed in {commit}”; German IDE: “Bitte mit aktuellem Build prüfen”, “Behoben in {commit}”), on, off, 10, assignedOrCreated, on, empty, 1920 | Plugin (registry `IssuesTracker`, `IssuesStart`, `IssuesBranchPattern`, `IssuesBranchBase`, `IssuesCommitPattern`, `TrackerLogin`, `IssuesQueryPicker`, `IssuesCreate`, `IssuesCreateIncludeCode`, `CreateIssueKey`, `IssuesPreview`, `IssuesPreviewComments`, `IssuesCodeLinks`, `IssuesBlameLinks`, `IssuesBlameMaxRevisions`, `IssuesSyncState`, `IssuesStateField`, `IssuesAssigneeField`, `IssuesStartState`, `IssuesAssignOnStart`, `IssuesStartComment`, `IssuesEndStates`, `IssuesEndComment`, `IssuesTimeTracking`, `IssuesIdleMinutes`, `IssuesTimeRounding`, `IssuesPreviewChecklists`, `IssuesChecklistStatus`, `IssuesPreviewLinks`, `IssuesWarnBlocked`, `IssuesBoard`, `IssuesBoardConfirmMove`, `IssuesBoardOnlyMine`, `IssuesSprintBurndown`, `IssuesSprintCompare`, `IssuesPaletteSearch`, `IssuesCommentEditor`, `IssuesCommentSnippets`, `IssuesPreviewDevelopment`, `IssuesNotify`, `IssuesNotifyIntervalMinutes`, `IssuesNotifyScope`, `IssuesAttach`, `IssuesAttachLogFiles`, `IssuesAttachMaxImageWidth`; `issues.connections`, `issues.projects` and `issues.queries` in settings.json; state of the messages per connection in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Atlas\issues\notify.json`) | no | Choice, choice, text field, text field, text field, checkbox, table, table, table, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, number, checkbox, drop-down list, drop-down list, drop-down list, checkbox, text field, text field, text field, checkbox, number (1–120), number (1–60), checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, checkbox, table, checkbox, checkbox, number (2–1440), choice, checkbox, text field, number (320–7680) | #765, #1280, #1260, #1261, #1262, #1268, #1264, #1265, #1275, #1266, #1267, #1273, #1279, #1272, #1277, #1270, #1278, #1269, #1271, #1276 |'
